# Microservice

Purpose: maintenance and operational endpoints, notably DB field-encryption key rotation/migration, using a schema subset aligned with those tasks.

Structure:
- server.ts — starts the service (H3/nitro style)
- routes/
  - migrate.get.ts, migrate.post.ts — migration/reencrypt triggers
  - test.get.ts — simple health/test route
- clients/ — prismaClient.ts and redisClient.ts
- prisma/ — schema.prisma (subset), migrations, reencrypt/
- lib/bull.ts — BullMQ helpers
- scripts/k8s-rotate-db-key.sh — used by the special key-rotation image to rotate secrets + call /migrate

Deployment:
- K8S Deployment runs the microservice on containerPort 3050 with a ClusterIP Service
- Receives INTERNAL_API_TOKEN via env; main app references MICROSERVICE_INTERNAL_URL for internal calls
- A second image target (runner-keyrotate) bundles kubectl and is used by a CronJob in staging for nightly key rotation

Notes:
- Keep models in microservice/prisma/schema.prisma consistent with app models it manages; it is not a full mirror
- Build uses microservice/copy-files.sh before docker build (seen in CI pre_build_command)
